statement:
For every \(r\ge2\), there is a finite \(K_4\)-free bouquet of \(r\)
permutation cycles such that:
1. every proper subbouquet is coherent;
2. the full bouquet is incoherent;
3. every constraint relation is a bijection;
4. every value is locally support-consistent.

Enumerate inclusion-minimal finite \(K_4\)-free fiber-coherence cores whose
incidence graph has one 2-connected block of cycle rank at least two.
Record:
1. deletion-debt spectrum from PG19;
2. minimum variable feedback sets and all PG07 forest certificates;
3. every cycle monodromy support;
4. overlap pattern of cycles inside the block;
5. whether incoherence is visible in a proper cactus sub-CSP.
Classify the first cores whose incoherence is intrinsic to the
2-connected block.
